/S /H3
/P 105 0 R
/T (The project analyses global petrol, diesel and LPG prices alongside income levels, subsidy structures and fuel-tax policies across 84 countries and 7 global regions from 2020 to 2026. The supplied brief describes 27,468 complete records and 10 variables. The intended output is an interactive business-intelligence solution that helps users compare fuel-price levels, examine changes over time, and explore how taxes, subsidies and income context relate to observed prices.)
/E (The project analyses global petrol, diesel and LPG prices alongside income levels, subsidy structures and fuel-tax policies across 84 countries and 7 global regions from 2020 to 2026. The supplied brief describes 27,468 complete records and 10 variables. The intended output is an interactive business-intelligence solution that helps users compare fuel-price levels, examine changes over time, and explore how taxes, subsidies and income context relate to observed prices.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [27]
>>
